NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000293 "1;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000294 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000295 "# ABSTRACT: Dispatches messages to one or more outputs"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000296 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000297 "__END__"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000298 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000299 "=pod"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000300 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000301 "=encoding UTF-8"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000302 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000303 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000304 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000305 "Log::Dispatch - Dispatches messages to one or more outputs"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000306 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000307 "=head1 VERSION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000308 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000309 "version 2.71"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000310 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000311 "=head1 SYNOPSIS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000312 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000313 "  use Log::Dispatch;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000314 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000315 "  # Simple API"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000316 "  #"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000317 "  my $log = Log::Dispatch->new("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000318 "      outputs => ["
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000319 "          [ 'File',   min_level => 'debug', filename => 'logfile' ],"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000320 "          [ 'Screen', min_level => 'warning' ],"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000321 "      ],"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000322 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000323 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000324 "  $log->info('Blah, blah');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000325 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000326 "  # More verbose API"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000327 "  #"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000328 "  my $log = Log::Dispatch->new();"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000329 "  $log->add("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000330 "      Log::Dispatch::File->new("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000331 "          name      => 'file1',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000332 "          min_level => 'debug',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000333 "          filename  => 'logfile'"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000334 "      )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000335 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000336 "  $log->add("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000337 "      Log::Dispatch::Screen->new("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000338 "          name      => 'screen',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000339 "          min_level => 'warning',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000340 "      )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000341 "  );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000342 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000343 "  $log->log( level => 'info', message => 'Blah, blah' );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000344 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000345 "  my $sub = sub { my %p = @_; return reverse $p{message}; };"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000346 "  my $reversing_dispatcher = Log::Dispatch->new( callbacks => $sub );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000347 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000348 "=head1 DESCRIPTION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000349 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000350 "This module manages a set of Log::Dispatch::* output objects that can be logged"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000351 "to via a unified interface."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000352 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000353 "The idea is that you create a Log::Dispatch object and then add various logging"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000354 "objects to it (such as a file logger or screen logger). Then you call the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000355 "C<log> method of the dispatch object, which passes the message to each of the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000356 "objects, which in turn decide whether or not to accept the message and what to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000357 "do with it."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000358 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000359 "This makes it possible to call single method and send a message to a log file,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000360 "via email, to the screen, and anywhere else, all with very little code needed"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000361 "on your part, once the dispatching object has been created."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000362 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000363 "=head1 METHODS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000364 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000365 "This class provides the following methods:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000366 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000367 "=head2 Log::Dispatch->new(...)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000368 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000369 "This method takes the following parameters:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000370 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000371 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000372 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000373 "=item * outputs( [ [ class, params, ... ], [ class, params, ... ], ... ] )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000374 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000375 "This parameter is a reference to a list of lists. Each inner list consists of a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000376 "class name and a set of constructor params. The class is automatically prefixed"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000377 "with 'Log::Dispatch::' unless it begins with '+', in which case the string"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000378 "following '+' is taken to be a full classname. e.g."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000379 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000380 "    outputs => [ [ 'File',          min_level => 'debug', filename => 'logfile' ],"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000381 "                 [ '+My::Dispatch', min_level => 'info' ] ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000382 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000383 "For each inner list, a new output object is created and added to the dispatcher"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000384 "(via the C<add()> method)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000385 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000386 "See L</\"OUTPUT CLASSES\"> for the parameters that can be used when creating an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000387 "output object."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000388 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000389 "=item * callbacks( \\& or [ \\&, \\&, ... ] )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000390 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000391 "This parameter may be a single subroutine reference or an array reference of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000392 "subroutine references. These callbacks will be called in the order they are"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000393 "given and passed a hash containing the following keys:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000394 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000395 " ( message => $log_message, level => $log_level )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000396 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000397 "In addition, any key/value pairs passed to a logging method will be passed onto"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000398 "your callback."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000399 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000400 "The callbacks are expected to modify the message and then return a single"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000401 "scalar containing that modified message. These callbacks will be called when"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000402 "either the C<log> or C<log_to> methods are called and will only be applied to a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000403 "given message once. If they do not return the message then you will get no"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000404 "output. Make sure to return the message!"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000405 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000406 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000407 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000408 "=head2 $dispatch->clone()"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000409 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000410 "This returns a I<shallow> clone of the original object. The underlying output"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000411 "objects and callbacks are shared between the two objects. However any changes"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000412 "made to the outputs or callbacks that the object contains are not shared."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000413 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000414 "=head2 $dispatch->log( level => $, message => $ or \\& )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000415 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000416 "Sends the message (at the appropriate level) to all the output objects that the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000417 "dispatcher contains (by calling the C<log_to> method repeatedly)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000418 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000419 "The level can be specified by name or by an integer from 0 (debug) to 7"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000420 "(emergency)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000421 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000422 "This method also accepts a subroutine reference as the message argument. This"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000423 "reference will be called only if there is an output that will accept a message"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000424 "of the specified level."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000425 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000426 "=head2 $dispatch->debug (message), info (message), ..."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000427 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000428 "You may call any valid log level (including valid abbreviations) as a method"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000429 "with a single argument that is the message to be logged. This is converted into"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000430 "a call to the C<log> method with the appropriate level."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000431 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000432 "For example:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000433 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000434 " $log->alert('Strange data in incoming request');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000435 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000436 "translates to:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000437 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000438 " $log->log( level => 'alert', message => 'Strange data in incoming request' );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000439 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000440 "If you pass an array to these methods, it will be stringified as is:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000441 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000442 " my @array = ('Something', 'bad', 'is', 'here');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000443 " $log->alert(@array);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000444 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000445 " # is equivalent to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000446 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000447 " $log->alert(\"@array\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000448 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000449 "You can also pass a subroutine reference, just like passing one to the C<log()>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000450 "method."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000451 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000452 "=head2 $dispatch->log_and_die( level => $, message => $ or \\& )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000453 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000454 "Has the same behavior as calling C<log()> but calls C<_die_with_message()> at"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000455 "the end."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000456 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000457 "You can throw exception objects by subclassing this method."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000458 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000459 "If the C<carp_level> parameter is present its value will be added to the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000460 "current value of C<$Carp::CarpLevel>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000461 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000462 "=head2 $dispatch->log_and_croak( level => $, message => $ or \\& )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000463 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000464 "A synonym for C<$dispatch->log_and_die()>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000465 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000466 "=head2 $dispatch->log_to( name => $, level => $, message => $ )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000467 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000468 "Sends the message only to the named object. Note: this will not properly handle"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000469 "a subroutine reference as the message."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000470 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000471 "=head2 $dispatch->add_callback( $code )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000472 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000473 "Adds a callback (like those given during construction). It is added to the end"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000474 "of the list of callbacks. Note that this can also be called on individual"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000475 "output objects."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000476 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000477 "=head2 $dispatch->remove_callback( $code )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000478 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000479 "Remove the given callback from the list of callbacks. Note that this can also"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000480 "be called on individual output objects."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000481 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000482 "=head2 $dispatch->callbacks()"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000483 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000484 "Returns a list of the callbacks in a given output."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000485 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000486 "=head2 $dispatch->level_is_valid( $string )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000487 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000488 "Returns true or false to indicate whether or not the given string is a valid"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000489 "log level. Can be called as either a class or object method."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000490 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000491 "=head2 $dispatch->would_log( $string )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000492 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000493 "Given a log level, returns true or false to indicate whether or not anything"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000494 "would be logged for that log level."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000495 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000496 "=head2 $dispatch->is_C<$level>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000497 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000498 "There are methods for every log level: C<is_debug()>, C<is_warning()>, etc."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000499 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000500 "This returns true if the logger will log a message at the given level."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000501 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000502 "=head2 $dispatch->add( Log::Dispatch::* OBJECT )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000503 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000504 "Adds a new L<output object|/\"OUTPUT CLASSES\"> to the dispatcher. If an object"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000505 "of the same name already exists, then that object is replaced, with a warning"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000506 "if C<$^W> is true."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000507 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000508 "=head2 $dispatch->remove($)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000509 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000510 "Removes the output object that matches the name given to the remove method. The"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000511 "return value is the object being removed or undef if no object matched this."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000512 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000513 "=head2 $dispatch->outputs()"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000514 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000515 "Returns a list of output objects."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000516 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000517 "=head2 $dispatch->output( $name )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000518 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000519 "Returns the output object of the given name. Returns undef or an empty list,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000520 "depending on context, if the given output does not exist."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000521 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000522 "=head2 $dispatch->_die_with_message( message => $, carp_level => $ )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000523 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000524 "This method is used by C<log_and_die> and will either die() or croak()"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000525 "depending on the value of C<message>: if it's a reference or it ends with a new"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000526 "line then a plain die will be used, otherwise it will croak."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000527 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000528 "=head1 OUTPUT CLASSES"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000529 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000530 "An output class - e.g. L<Log::Dispatch::File> or L<Log::Dispatch::Screen> -"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000531 "implements a particular way of dispatching logs. Many output classes come with"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000532 "this distribution, and others are available separately on CPAN."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000533 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000534 "The following common parameters can be used when creating an output class. All"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000535 "are optional. Most output classes will have additional parameters beyond these,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000536 "see their documentation for details."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000537 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000538 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000539 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000540 "=item * name ($)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000541 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000542 "A name for the object (not the filename!). This is useful if you want to refer"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000543 "to the object later, e.g. to log specifically to it or remove it."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000544 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000545 "By default a unique name will be generated. You should not depend on the form"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000546 "of generated names, as they may change."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000547 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000548 "=item * min_level ($)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000549 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000550 "The minimum L<logging level|/\"LOG LEVELS\"> this object will accept. Required."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000551 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000552 "=item * max_level ($)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000553 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000554 "The maximum L<logging level|/\"LOG LEVELS\"> this object will accept. By default"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000555 "the maximum is the highest possible level (which means functionally that the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000556 "object has no maximum)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000557 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000558 "=item * callbacks( \\& or [ \\&, \\&, ... ] )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000559 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000560 "This parameter may be a single subroutine reference or an array reference of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000561 "subroutine references. These callbacks will be called in the order they are"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000562 "given and passed a hash containing the following keys:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000563 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000564 " ( message => $log_message, level => $log_level )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000565 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000566 "The callbacks are expected to modify the message and then return a single"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000567 "scalar containing that modified message. These callbacks will be called when"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000568 "either the C<log> or C<log_to> methods are called and will only be applied to a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000569 "given message once. If they do not return the message then you will get no"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000570 "output. Make sure to return the message!"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000571 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000572 "=item * newline (0|1)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000573 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000574 "If true, a callback will be added to the end of the callbacks list that adds a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000575 "newline to the end of each message. Default is false, but some output classes"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000576 "may decide to make the default true."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000577 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000578 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000579 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000580 "=head1 LOG LEVELS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000581 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000582 "The log levels that Log::Dispatch uses are taken directly from the syslog man"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000583 "pages (except that I expanded them to full words). Valid levels are:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000584 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000585 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000586 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000587 "=item debug"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000588 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000589 "=item info"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000590 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000591 "=item notice"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000592 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000593 "=item warning"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000594 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000595 "=item error"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000596 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000597 "=item critical"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000598 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000599 "=item alert"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000600 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000601 "=item emergency"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000602 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000603 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000604 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000605 "Alternately, the numbers 0 through 7 may be used (debug is 0 and emergency is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000606 "7). The syslog standard of 'err', 'crit', and 'emerg' is also acceptable. We"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000607 "also allow 'warn' as a synonym for 'warning'."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000608 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000609 "=head1 SUBCLASSING"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000610 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000611 "This module was designed to be easy to subclass. If you want to handle"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000612 "messaging in a way not implemented in this package, you should be able to add"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000613 "this with minimal effort. It is generally as simple as subclassing"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000614 "Log::Dispatch::Output and overriding the C<new> and C<log_message> methods. See"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000615 "the L<Log::Dispatch::Output> docs for more details."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000616 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000617 "If you would like to create your own subclass for sending email then it is even"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000618 "simpler. Simply subclass L<Log::Dispatch::Email> and override the C<send_email>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000619 "method. See the L<Log::Dispatch::Email> docs for more details."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000620 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000621 "The logging levels that Log::Dispatch uses are borrowed from the standard UNIX"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000622 "syslog levels, except that where syslog uses partial words (\"err\")"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000623 "Log::Dispatch also allows the use of the full word as well (\"error\")."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000624 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000625 "=head1 RELATED MODULES"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000626 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000627 "=head2 Log::Dispatch::DBI"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000628 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000629 "Written by Tatsuhiko Miyagawa. Log output to a database table."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000630 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000631 "=head2 Log::Dispatch::FileRotate"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000632 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000633 "Written by Mark Pfeiffer. Rotates log files periodically as part of its usage."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000634 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000635 "=head2 Log::Dispatch::File::Stamped"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000636 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000637 "Written by Eric Cholet. Stamps log files with date and time information."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000638 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000639 "=head2 Log::Dispatch::Jabber"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000640 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000641 "Written by Aaron Straup Cope. Logs messages via Jabber."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000642 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000643 "=head2 Log::Dispatch::Tk"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000644 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000645 "Written by Dominique Dumont. Logs messages to a Tk window."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000646 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000647 "=head2 Log::Dispatch::Win32EventLog"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000648 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000649 "Written by Arthur Bergman. Logs messages to the Windows event log."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000650 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000651 "=head2 Log::Log4perl"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000652 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000653 "An implementation of Java's log4j API in Perl. Log messages can be limited by"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000654 "fine-grained controls, and if they end up being logged, both native Log4perl"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000655 "and Log::Dispatch appenders can be used to perform the actual logging job."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000656 "Created by Mike Schilli and Kevin Goess."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000657 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000658 "=head2 Log::Dispatch::Config"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000659 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000660 "Written by Tatsuhiko Miyagawa. Allows configuration of logging via a text file"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000661 "similar (or so I'm told) to how it is done with log4j. Simpler than"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000662 "Log::Log4perl."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000663 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000664 "=head2 Log::Agent"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000665 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000666 "A very different API for doing many of the same things that Log::Dispatch does."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000667 "Originally written by Raphael Manfredi."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000668 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000669 "=head1 SEE ALSO"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000670 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000671 "L<Log::Dispatch::ApacheLog>, L<Log::Dispatch::Email>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000672 "L<Log::Dispatch::Email::MailSend>, L<Log::Dispatch::Email::MailSender>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000673 "L<Log::Dispatch::Email::MailSendmail>, L<Log::Dispatch::Email::MIMELite>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000674 "L<Log::Dispatch::File>, L<Log::Dispatch::File::Locked>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000675 "L<Log::Dispatch::Handle>, L<Log::Dispatch::Output>, L<Log::Dispatch::Screen>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000676 "L<Log::Dispatch::Syslog>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000677 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000678 "=head1 SUPPORT"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000679 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000680 "Bugs may be submitted at L<https://github.com/houseabsolute/Log-Dispatch/issues>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000681 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000682 "=head1 SOURCE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000683 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000684 "The source code repository for Log-Dispatch can be found at L<https://github.com/houseabsolute/Log-Dispatch>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000685 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000686 "=head1 DONATIONS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000687 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000688 "If you'd like to thank me for the work I've done on this module, please"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000689 "consider making a \"donation\" to me via PayPal. I spend a lot of free time"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000690 "creating free software, and would appreciate any support you'd care to offer."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000691 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000692 "Please note that B<I am not suggesting that you must do this> in order for me"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000693 "to continue working on this particular software. I will continue to do so,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000694 "inasmuch as I have in the past, for as long as it interests me."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000695 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000696 "Similarly, a donation made in this way will probably not make me work on this"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000697 "software much more, unless I get so many donations that I can consider working"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000698 "on free software full time (let's all have a chuckle at that together)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000699 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000700 "To donate, log into PayPal and send money to autarch@urth.org, or use the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000701 "button at L<https://houseabsolute.com/foss-donations/>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000702 ""
